Package: herdr-app
Version: herdr_app_VERSION-BUILD_VERSION~griffo
Architecture: SUPPORTED_ARCHITECTURES
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35), libgcc-s1, libxcb1, libxkbcommon0, libxkbcommon-x11-0, libfontconfig1, libvulkan1, libegl1, libwayland-client0, libwayland-egl1, curl, xdg-utils, herdr-core (>= CORE_MIN)
Recommends: mesa-vulkan-drivers, pulseaudio-utils | pipewire-bin, openssh-client
Description: desktop app for terminals and coding agents
 Herdr keeps terminal work in spaces, usually one per repository, each with
 tabs split into panes. An agents sidebar gathers the coding agents running
 in every space and shows which are working, blocked waiting for you, or
 done. Closing the window leaves the terminals running, and SSH machines can
 be added so a space runs its terminals on another computer.
 .
 The command is herdr-app. Terminals run in herdr-core, installed with it
 from the herdr-core package. Herdr needs a desktop session (X11 or Wayland)
 and a working Vulkan driver. Its own self-updater is off in this package;
 updates to both come through apt.
